d of knew what was  going on so it was targeting them  finding the ones that were really  struggling didn't know how to properly  manage the property or had some other  problem and just being able to help  solve it that's excellent fantastic so  when did you start out doing this so  it's been just about four years yes what  does what does your strategy consists of  now do you still do regiments um we do  we don't do loads of advertising so most  of ours come through word-of-mouth now  or properties our landlords have more  properties and they pass them on to us  so I've got a small team that manages  the rent to rent portfolio so we're  pretty happy with how that's going and  don't do those of advertising we've  bought a couple of our own properties as  well now so we own a few in Oxford and  and in some of the surrounding areas and  recently our newest strategy is we've  just bought 27 acres of land where we  are going to start a farm so we're not  gonna do a big development on it we're  going to have our own alpaca farm so  that was kind of one of our dreams oh we  first oh yes right yeah but that's the  thing property is a vehicle and being  able to have of your own bread to rent  portfolio you've bought a couple of  houses and  investments now you can start to do that  kind of thing exactly exactly and we've  got kind of the connections we need  because it's basically just a proper  blank field so we're thinking of doing a  bit of container storage on there so I'm  gonna meet with a few people that do  that strategy that I've met through the  different property networks and we might  do some glamping pods and stuff but I've  got I know the people to kind of help us  with that now so it's awesome so what  would you say your average week looks  like now ah so there it's it's  relatively relaxed I probably spend  about 10 hours a week working on my  property business so on the managing the  actual properties because I've got a  team that does it so most of it is you  know meeting with them making sure  they're on track and that they don't  have any huge questions the rest of the  time I do coaching and mentoring so  about quite a few online programs and  working with kind of private clients and  then it's just relaxing and setting up  the farm is basically with yes I heard a  quote and it said if you do in the early  days what most people aren't prepared to  then you'll be able to do in the later  days what most people can't do exactly  and the fact you've got that place yes  because it was hard work in the  beginning I spent a lot of time I mean  my social life went down I was spending  more time you know working my property  business than I had been on my normal  job my friends had no idea what on earth  I was doing they thought I was a crazy  person  but now I've got I've got all my time  back basically so we travel quite a bit  I'm able to kind of go away and be away  for weeks at a time and and everything  still runs without me because the great  thing about rental rents a guess is the  fact that and most mostly in property is  you do it once and you get paid ongoing  yeah it's all about cashflow passive  income which is which is really exciting  so what are your plans for the future  then besides the farm yeah that's pretty  much the big one  yeah because there's so many things I  mean 27 acres is pretty huge there's so  many different things we can do on there  so yeah we've got to put a tell puckers  now we've got a build up to 30 is the  goal and we've got bunnies and yeah we  do the glamping pot that's gonna be  awesome so that's my I do change  I do get bored quite easily so I might  be into something else in the year but  right now that's that's the big plan and  it is it's setting up that lifestyle  business for us was the goal so that's  the lifestyle work well congratulations  if I know you've been successful in what  you've done but if you were to speak to  your four years younger self who was  just finishing up with accountancy what  piece of advice one piece of advice  would you give them I would say focus so  when I first first got started before we  really decided on rent to rent I tried  to do every property strategy so I did a  training course one of those three-day  courses where you learn all the  strategies and I was like I'm a property  investor I'm gonna do all of them and I  spent six months running around like a  crazy person trying to do every strategy  and I got absolutely nowhere and it  wasn't until I said all right what are  my goals what am i focusing on that that  I was able to kind of build up that  momentum and get a proper business going  right yeah great advice fantastic and  today you've been with my certified palm  how was that oh that was excellent it's  a really good group of people so we  covered a good in-depth session on rent  to rent they asked loads of really  really good questions and I think they  went away with a lot of information to  actually get out there and start getting  the rent to rent good implementation  yeah as you probably right so I saw that  because they mean loads of them have  done loads of deals and they're getting  lots of sourcing and yeah yeah yeah and  and now we're off to the property  investor circle which is really good to  be excited so thanks thanks so much for  coming on the show and how would we  contact you I mean I would say whoever's  watching this you need to get Jackie's  book so if you just search what's the  name of the book rent search renter rent  on Amazon and my books will come up I've  got two of them right and how would  anyone get in touch with you if they  want to you know email you or give you a  chat with the self the best place to  find me is probably rent to rent Academy  code UK is my main rent to rent website  and that's got kind of contact form and  it's got loads of loads and loads of  information on rent to rent on there so  that's the best place to go so rent to  rent Academy code at